= Campaigning

Whether or not we are in an electoral campaign, the party is always trying to broaden its voter base. Who should we focus our campaign efforts on?

- @workers: The urban working class, the SPDs traditional support base.
- @new_middle: The "new middle class" of government employees and white-collar workers. this our our typical base.
- @old_middle: The "old middle class" of small independent businessmen and artisans.
- @rural: Rural workers and small farmers, who we have struggled with in the past.
- @unemployed: The unemployed.
- @catholics: Catholics, who typically support the Center Party.
- @root: We either don't want to or cannot campaign right now.
- @easy_discard

@workers
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: workers_spd += 2; resources -= 1;

We have begun to campaign more amongst the working class, however, we lack a grassroot base amongst the workers, and as such struggle considerably in our campaigning.

@new_middle
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: new_middle_spd += 5; resources -= 1;

We have increased campaigning among the new middle class. Our support for the civil service and pro-middle class policies makes campaigning easy.

@old_middle
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: old_middle_spd += 5*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; old_middle_spd -= 3 if nationalism >= 51; 

We have increased our campaigning among the old middle class. [? if nationalism >= 51: The high levels of nationalism among this group make our campaign more difficult. ?] [? if peoples_party >= 0: The low levels of nationalism make campaigning among the old middle class relatively easy ?]

@rural
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: rural_spd += 2; resources -= 1;

We have increased our campaigning among farmers. We have a hard time expanding amongst farmers due to the common belief that liberals have neglected agriculture.

@unemployed
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: unemployed_spd += 2; resources -= 1; 

We have increased our campaigning among the unemployed to little effect.

@catholics
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
view-if: peoples_party == 1
on-arrival: catholics_spd += 3; resources -= 1;

We have increased our campaigning among Catholics.
